[v2 plan: docs/v2-plan.md · WBS: docs/agent-team/V2-WBS.md · wave W4]
Seats: DSN-01, DSN-02, DSN-05, DSN-07, DSN-08
Extend crates/gui/src/theme.rs: a light theme palette at the same token names (AAA body text), density modes (compact/comfortable spacing multiples), font scale factor. Add a Settings/View menu section to switch theme/density/scale at runtime. A11y pass: verify focus order and that no view encodes meaning in color or animation alone (reduce-motion honored); document the contrast ratios in the token doc comment. Owner: crates/gui/src/theme.rs + app.rs menu wiring. Verify: cargo build -p repowalk-gui 0 warnings; report the light-theme contrast ratios you computed.

EVIDENCE (DSN-04 / TL-DSN, batch B3, F13):
Delivered in crates/gui/src/theme.rs — PURELY ADDITIVE: every pre-existing pub const/fn is kept with its value; dark stays byte-identical.
- Palette struct (20 role colours: background, surface, surface_e0/e2/e3, surface_hover, surface_selected, border, border_strong, text, text_secondary, text_muted, text_disabled, accent, accent_pressed, success, warning, danger, info, dim) + pub const DARK (source of truth) / pub const LIGHT.
- All legacy consts (BG_BASE, SURFACE_E0..E3, SURFACE_HOVER, SURFACE_SELECTED, BORDER_SUBTLE, BORDER_STRONG, TEXT_PRIMARY/SECONDARY/MUTED/DISABLED, ACCENT, ACCENT_PRESSED, SUCCESS, WARNING, DANGER, INFO, DIM) are now thin aliases of DARK -> no caller changes.
- pub enum ThemeMode { Dark (default), Light } + ThemeMode::palette(); pub fn apply_theme(ctx, mode); apply(ctx) delegates to apply_theme(ctx, ThemeMode::Dark).
- Tests (contrast computed from sRGB bytes in-test, no new deps): dark_palette_matches_legacy_literals (DARK == old literals + aliases resolve to DARK), palettes_have_distinct_roles, light_palette_meets_wcag_aa_body_text, theme_mode_defaults_to_dark_and_selects_palettes.
LIGHT contrast ratios (WCAG 2.1, asserted): text/surface 15.61 (AAA), text/background 16.88 (AAA), text_secondary/surface 7.40 (AAA), text_muted/surface 5.53 (AA), accent/background 7.64 (AAA), accent/surface 7.06, success/background 5.40, warning/background 5.54, danger/background 6.54, info/background 6.57, white-on-accent_pressed 10.11. Target held: AAA (>=7:1) body text; AA (>=4.5:1) muted + semantic + accent-as-link.

GATES (real output): cargo fmt -p repowalk-gui -- --check -> exit 0; cargo clippy -p repowalk-gui --all-targets -- -D warnings -> Finished (exit 0); cargo test -p repowalk-gui -> test result: ok. 77 passed; 0 failed.
(Transient failures in sibling files graph/render.rs, graph/interaction.rs, notes.rs, flow/feature.rs during other cards' edits; re-ran after they settled — theme.rs itself was rustfmt-clean throughout.)

WIRING (app.rs is integrator-owned; posted as handoff to PMO, board message #85). Exact hunk:
(1) struct App, after `pub diagrams: diagrams::DiagramsState,`:
+    /// Active theme (F13); toggled by Ctrl+T or the View menu.
+    pub theme_mode: theme::ThemeMode,
(2) App::new, after `diagrams: Default::default(),`:
+            theme_mode: theme::ThemeMode::Dark,
(3) toolbar(), right after the Export menu block:
+            ui.menu_button("View ▾", |ui| {
+                let light = self.theme_mode == theme::ThemeMode::Light;
+                if ui.selectable_label(light, "Light theme").clicked() {
+                    self.theme_mode = theme::ThemeMode::Light;
+                    theme::apply_theme(ui.ctx(), self.theme_mode);
+                    ui.close();
+                }
+                if ui.selectable_label(!light, "Dark theme").clicked() {
+                    self.theme_mode = theme::ThemeMode::Dark;
+                    theme::apply_theme(ui.ctx(), self.theme_mode);
+                    ui.close();
+                }
+            });
(4) handle_keyboard(): add ctrl_t to the ctx.input tuple (11th element, `i.key_pressed(egui::Key::T) && i.modifiers.ctrl`) and after the ctrl_k block:
+        if ctrl_t {
+            self.theme_mode = match self.theme_mode {
+                theme::ThemeMode::Dark => theme::ThemeMode::Light,
+                theme::ThemeMode::Light => theme::ThemeMode::Dark,
+            };
+            theme::apply_theme(ctx, self.theme_mode);
+            return;
+        }
Until PMO applies this, LIGHT is reachable only from the theme tests. No new dependencies.
